## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, scalable controls under wild traffic spikes, balancing reliability and user impact. It probes knowledge of where to enforce limits, how to define quotas, and how to implement safe degradation with measurable rollback criteria.

## Key Concepts
- Rate limiting and quotas (gateway vs mesh)
- Backends under backpressure and load shedding
- Degradation paths and cache fallbacks
- Observability: p95 latency, error rate, saturation
- Rollback criteria and safety valves

